From b1ff43e049541b83b958fa8325a23f0b30d0643e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snap-pea <snap-pea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:48:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/19] opencl: row-per-lane flash-decoding kernel for q8_0 KV,
 dk=256, GQA 8

flash_attn_f32_q8_0_q1_vec_mq_split reduces every KV row across the subgroup once
per head (8 serial reductions per row) and runs at ~20 GB/s at depth. The new
kernel_fa_q8_d256_g8_dec gives each lane a whole KV row for QK (dp4a against Q
requantized to int8 in local memory), reduces softmax statistics once per 64-row
tile, and has each lane own 4 of the 256 output dims for PV. Same arguments and
partial records as the MQ split kernel, so the host dispatch and merge are reused.

X2-90, Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, q8_0 KV, tg32: d0 32.7 -> 32.6, d8192 27.4 -> 31.0,
d32768 20.3 -> 27.7. test-backend-ops FLASH_ATTN_EXT 2985/2985 OK.
Opt out: GGML_OPENCL_FA_Q8_D256_LPR=0. Also adds dk=256 q8_0 GQA8 decode test cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
